# runner: kill-restart-after 3
#
# Server loss and recovery. The server is killed *externally* while the client
# is connected: the client notices the closed socket, goes Lost with the
# Structural Mirror and Project Replica frozen, and a `reconnect` to a
# restarted server bootstraps it again.
#
# The first line is a hint for run_scenario.sh: once the client has printed
# three `OK` records (connect and the two asserts below), the runner kills the
# server, waits for it to exit, and starts a fresh one on the same port. The
# `sleep` gives the restart time to reach Listening before `reconnect`, which
# makes one attempt and does not retry. Without the runner (a plain
# `--script` run) `await-lost` FAILs after 20 s because nothing kills the
# server; this scenario is registered with ctest through the runner only.

connect
assert state == Connected
assert scene.objects >= 1

# The runner kills the server now.
await-lost timeout=20000
assert state == Lost

# Lost keeps the last known state as a frozen view...
assert scene.objects >= 1
assert project.shots >= 1

# ...and the runner has restarted the server meanwhile.
sleep 3000
reconnect timeout=10000
assert state == Connected
assert scene.objects >= 1
assert project.shots >= 1
ping
expect-pong

shutdown
assert state == Disconnected
